 <h2 class="text-lg font-black uppercase text-amber-700 mb-3">Key Takeaways</h2>
 <ul class="text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
 <li><strong>3 non-negotiable factory verification steps</strong>: (1) video call walkthrough of the production floor, match the background to photos on their website; (2) request 3 recent customer references in your target market, not just generic testimonials; (3) verify at least one active certification (CE/FCC/UL) on the issuing body's public database, not just a PDF.</li>
 <li><strong>MOQ negotiation sweet spot: 500-1,000 units for private-label chargers</strong> with existing tooling. First order: expect to pay 30% deposit, 70% before shipment. Subsequent orders: negotiate to 30/70 or net-30 terms after 3 successful orders.</li>
 <li><strong>Factory audit red flags</strong>: refusal to share BOM with FET part numbers, "we can do everything" without specialization, quotes 50% below market average, no English-speaking quality engineer, and reluctance to do a live video tour. Walk away from any factory that hits 3+ of these.</li>
 <li><strong>Timeline: 25-30 days from sample approval to production completion</strong> for OEM orders using existing tooling. ODM with new mold tooling: 45-60 days. Samples: 3-7 days. Sea freight to EU/US: 25-35 days. Total door-to-door: plan 10-12 weeks for a first order. Rush orders available.</li>
 </ul>
