 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-4">1. OEM Sourcing: Initial Research & Shortlisting</h2>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">The first step is knowing where to look and what criteria to use for initial screening. A structured approach saves weeks of wasted communication with unsuitable suppliers. Start your supplier search with these channels:</p>
 <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 mb-4">
 <li><strong>B2B platforms</strong>, Alibaba, Global Sources, Made-in-China for initial vetting</li>
 <li><strong>Trade shows</strong>, Canton Fair (Guangzhou), CES (Las Vegas), electronica (Munich)</li>
 <li><strong>Industry referrals</strong>, Ask your network for supplier recommendations</li>
 <li><strong>Direct outreach</strong>, Contact Shenzhen factories directly via their websites</li>
 </ul>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Look for suppliers with at least 5+ years in business, verified factory audits (BV/SGS/TUV), and clear OEM/ODM case studies on their website. A professional B2B supplier website with detailed product specs, certification information, and company history is a strong sign of a legitimate manufacturer. It's much less likely to be a trading company. <a href="/products/power-bank/semi-solid-state/" class="text-brandBlue font-bold hover:text-brandOrange transition">Browse our semi-solid-state power bank lineup →</a></p>

