 <section id="faq" class="mb-16 p-8 bg-slate-50 rounded-3xl">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">China charger supplier verification spans four interconnected domains every OEM buyer must control: <strong>supplier discovery</strong> (B2B platforms, trade shows, industry referrals), <strong>factory legitimacy</strong> (ISO 9001 audits, video tours, third-party inspection), <strong>commercial terms</strong> (MOQ 500-3,000, FOB pricing tiers, 30/70 payment), and <strong>quality infrastructure</strong> (IQC→IPQC→FQC→OQC with 4-hour burn-in). Only 12% of electronics suppliers on B2B platforms pass comprehensive third-party audits, making independent verification non-negotiable before committing any deposit.</p>
 <div class="space-y-6">
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How do OEM buyers find a reliable charger supplier in China?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Start with verified B2B platforms (Alibaba Gold Supplier, Global Sources), check for ISO 9001 certification, request factory video tours, and always order samples before bulk purchases.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What is the standard MOQ for Chinese charger factories?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">MOQ varies by product type. Standard ODM models start at 500 units (WOWOHCOOL, Allway), while OEM custom projects typically require 1,000-3,000 units due to tooling costs.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How can OEM buyers verify a China factory is legitimate?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Request a video call factory tour, check their business license, verify ISO certifications, search for reviews on sourcing forums, and consider third-party audit services like SGS or BV.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What's the difference between a factory and a trading company?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">A factory owns production lines and can show you their manufacturing process. A trading company sources from multiple factories and adds a margin. Trading companies aren't always bad, but you'll get better pricing and QC control directly from the manufacturer.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How do OEM buyers get pricing and samples from a verified charger factory?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Request a quote from <a href="/contact/" class="text-brandBlue hover:text-brandOrange underline">WOWOHCOOL's OEM team</a>. Our ISO 9001 factory in Shenzhen offers MOQ from 500 units, 3-7 day sample turnaround, FOB pricing at 1,000 units from $3-14 depending on wattage, and full CE/FCC/RoHS certification documentation. All quotes include a complete BOM with component brands and a video factory tour within 24 hours of request.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>

 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-8">
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Choosing the right China charger supplier is one of the most important decisions for your product brand. Time invested in proper factory verification, sample testing, and transparent communication pays dividends in product quality and reliable delivery. WOWOHCOOL has been helping global brands navigate China sourcing since 2013 with ISO 9001 certified production and complete OEM/ODM support.</p>
